MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_001: Hey, Cai. I hear your reason for entering the\nHeroic Games is to save your dad?
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_002: Yeah. He's an annoying old geezer, but he's my pop.\nI can't just let him die.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_003: For sure. Well, I'm gonna help you! I know you and\nme can win it together.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_004: Yeah... Well, I know we're not on the same side,\nbut I'm pulling for you.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_005: Thanks! I appreciate that. But why did you want to\nknow about Pop?
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_006: I guess it's because I kinda relate? See, my dad's\nmissing, and I've been looking for him.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_007: When I was six years old, my mom kicked him out of\nthe house.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_008: Oh... Why'd she do that?
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_009: I don't know. Mom never wanted to say.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_010: What I do know is that my dad doted on me. I loved\nthe guy—and then one day, he was gone.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_011: It was sudden for me too. One day it was just, "Hey,\nwe're executing your father."
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_012: Why do parents try to hide this stuff from their kids?
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_013: No idea. It's so selfish! Do they think for one second\nabout how we feel?
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_014: And I mean... *sigh* I have no clue where my dad is.\nHe might already be dead.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_015: Don't talk like that. For all you know, he's out there\nlooking for you right now.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_016: You think so? Then how come he never came home?
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_017: Look, don't worry about it so much. I'm pulling for\nyou too, you know.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_018: Anyway, your name will get around because of the\nHeroic Games. He'll probably come and find you.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_019: Yeah... Yeah! You're right. And that means I don't\nhave time to get down in the dumps!
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_020: Thanks, Cai. Hehe. I came here to say I was pulling\nfor you, but it went the other way around.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_C_021: We'll call it even, because I'm feeling pretty good\nmyself. So let's give the games everything we've got!
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_001: You're still up, Mu? You should get to bed. We've\ngot an early day tomorrow.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_002: Right, sorry. Had something on my mind. I was\nwondering where my dad might be again.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_003: Hmmm... You know, maybe I can ask some of my\ntemple contacts if they can find him.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_004: Centurio's got a real gift for tracking. He might be\nable to pick up the trail at least.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_005: No, no. That's sweet. But with the world at war,\nI think you've got more pressing things to deal with.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_006: And I can watch out for myself. I'm too old to go\naround sobbing just 'cause my parents aren't around.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_007: We've grown up a lot, haven't we? Makes me miss\nthe old days. I thought you were a boy then!
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_008: Hmhm. Well. I was dressed for the part!
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_009: I really did hate her, my mom. I couldn't forgive her\nfor driving my dad away.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_010: That changed when I ran into one of his old buddies\nand asked him about my dad. Know what he said?
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_011: "The man—he liked his fine spirits." Guess that's\nwhere our family's budget went.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_012: Mm.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_013: That's why, when I asked my mom, all she could\nsay was "forget about it." She was protecting me.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_014: I'm too embarrassed to thank her to her face,\nsince we're always fighting.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_015: Then stop fighting and tell her. It's never too late.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_016: I was too embarrassed to thank her to her face,\nsince we were always fighting.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_017: You can tell her that whenever you visit her grave.\nI'm sure that'd make her happy.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_018: I used to fight with Pop all the time too. But I slowly\nstarted to realize that parenting is hard work.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_019: He had friends helping him, but I think raising a kid\nis always a challenge.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_020: Yeah... I thought my parents were selfish. But they\nwere just people trying their best in hard times.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_021: I do like the idea of it. Getting married, settling\ndown—when there's peace.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_022: Having families... For all the hard times we've been\nthrough, we'll spend as much time laughing.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_023: Let's get through this alive and put the world back in\norder so we can make that dream of yours come true.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_024: Hehe. Cai, this is striking a familiar note.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_025: Right. Back in the Heroic Games we talked about\ngiving it everything we've got.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_026: But this time we'll give everything we've got for a\nhappily ever after.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_027: Fair enough! Take Balor down, and then introduce\neach other to our new marriage partners.
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_028: And if you've got any gripes or complaints, I'll hear\nyou out!
MID_SE_Kai_Moo_B_029: And I'll listen to your complaints too. We'll make it\nour secret.